# 37. Store Scope

Every request must establish:

```text
Authenticated User
        ↓
Platform Authorization
        ↓
Vendor Authorization
        ↓
Store Authorization
        ↓
Domain Access
```

Never rely on route-level `storeId` alone.

---

# 38. Cross-Domain Rules

Store Details must call:

```text
Catalog → Catalog services
Inventory → Inventory services
Orders → Order services
POS → POS services
Payment → Payment services
Shipping → Shipping services
Tax → Tax services
SEO → SEO services
CMS → CMS services
Notifications → Notification services
Analytics → Analytics services
GEM → GEM services
```

Do not access another module's database directly.

---

# 39. Read Model

The Overview should use a dedicated read/aggregation model where beneficial.

Example:

```typescript
interface StoreOverview {
  store: StoreSummary;
  health: StoreHealth;
  sales: StoreSalesMetrics;
  inventory: StoreInventoryMetrics;
  operations: StoreOperationalMetrics;
  marketing: StoreMarketingMetrics;
}
```

The read model may aggregate data from multiple bounded contexts.

It must not become a second source of truth.

